# wfg-log 1
# fixture lane - a media cue's level lane redrawn, refused, cleared and put back
# (namespace draft §20).
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR: that a session in which the waveform's hands drew on a media
# cue's level lane - one node.set of the whole list per gesture, through the
# document's own door - reproduces exactly, refusals included. What a lane does
# to a LEVEL is not in this file and cannot be, for fade-curve's reason: §3.15
# keeps the fifty values a second out of the log, a replay runs no tick hooks,
# and the level a lane rides is checked in GoTests and heard by
# blackbox/lane_level.py instead. Recorded from a real `wfg serve` of
# tests/fixtures/bundles/lane driven over OSC with no audio device; the header
# lines below are the session's own.
#
# bundle lane sha256:e21ff8ebde68e3b7964dd93804683d84abdeb682258d5bf2f3b17332e827b058
# clock sampleRate=48000 blockSize=128 samplesPerTick=960
# media tone.wav 0 0.000
#
# THE FIRST CUE'S LANE REDRAWN: the ramp now goes down to -30 by the second
# second, held, and back at the sixth. One datagram carrying the whole list, as
# the waveform sends it when a drag lets go.
A 26 0 udp:127.0.0.1:49752 node.set s:"/godot/cue/VC000002/levelLane" s:"1 0 2 -30 6 -30 6.001 0"
#
# THREE DRAWINGS THE DOOR WOULD NOT TAKE, each with the reason it deserves, and
# the lane drawn a moment ago stays. A point missing its level: every element a
# number, so the type was right, and together not a lane - `bad-value`.
R 41 1 udp:127.0.0.1:49753 bad-value node.set s:"/godot/cue/VC000002/levelLane" s:"1 0 2"
#
# A level no cue may be written at (-120..12, the cue's own level row): `bad-value`.
R 56 2 udp:127.0.0.1:49754 bad-value node.set s:"/godot/cue/VC000002/levelLane" s:"1 0 2 -130"
#
# And a word where a number goes, the wrong KIND of thing: `type-mismatch`.
R 71 3 udp:127.0.0.1:49755 type-mismatch node.set s:"/godot/cue/VC000002/levelLane" s:"1 0 2 later"
#
# THE LOOP'S LANE CLEARED - the last point double-clicked away - and the undo
# that puts it back: a lane is a decision, so it is one step of the show's
# history like any other row.
A 86 4 udp:127.0.0.1:49756 node.set s:"/godot/cue/VC000005/levelLane" s:""
A 101 5 udp:127.0.0.1:49758 undo s:"document" s:"node.set"
#
# A MEMO HAS NO LANE: the row is a media cue's (§20.2), so its address does not
# exist on anything else - `bad-address`, not a lane quietly ignored.
R 116 6 udp:127.0.0.1:49763 bad-address node.set s:"/godot/cue/VC000008/levelLane" s:"0 -6"
